<title>GERMANY: German cocoa imports down in January at 15,263 T.</title>
<headline>German cocoa imports down in January at 15,263 T.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>German cocoa bean imports from third countries in January 1997 totalled 15,263 tonnes after 17,965 tonnes in December 1996 and 17,009 in January 1996, federal statistics office data showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>January import value was 35.43 million marks compared with 37.32 million the year before.</p>
<p>Leading supplier was Ivory Coast with 9,248 tonnes, followed by Ghana with 1,964, Nigeria with 1,450 and Indonesia's 968 tonnes.</p>
<p>Imports from third countries in 1996 totalled 303,853 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
